{
  "name": "pre-onboarding-rate-then-unset-then-onboarding",
  "group": "fx",
  "note": "conformance/fx: The shape that carries BOTH halves of the pre-onboarding problem at once, and which no other case reaches: a rate for the currency that becomes home, a row frozen against it, that rate then unset, a second row left pending, and only then the onboarding op \u2014 which installs the identity, backfills the pending row and raises the anomaly. t1 keeps its 2.0 basis and t2 gets the identity, so the two-basis split the anomaly reports is visible in the snapshots themselves. The anomaly fires on a NULL head, which is why the guard keys on 'a rate head exists' rather than on 'a non-null rate head exists'.",
